# CS4440 Project 2: Concurrency and Synchronization
## Hardware-Aware Implementation for Intel Xeon Sapphire Rapids

## Project Overview

This project implements three classic concurrency problems using POSIX pthread and semaphore primitives. Each implementation includes comprehensive hardware-aware comments that explain the end-to-end execution flow from user code through the operating system kernel to the CPU hardware.

**Educational Focus:**
- Connect POSIX synchronization primitives to real hardware execution
- Explain Intel Xeon Sapphire Rapids CPU architecture features
- Demonstrate cache coherency (MESI protocol) in multi-threaded programs
- Show complete execution flow: user code → glibc → kernel → CPU
- Provide insights for CTOs and engineers on OS/hardware interaction

